Syntax: cook <cookware> <recipe>

The cook skill allows you to prepare food items from raw ingredients. Cooking 
transforms basic food items into more complex dishes that often provide 
additional benefits when consumed.

To cook successfully:
- You must have the necessary ingredients in your inventory
- You need appropriate cookware (pot, pan, etc.)
- You must place the necessary ingredients in the cookware
- You need sufficient skill level for the recipe's difficulty

Recipes are categorized by difficulty:

TASK_TRIVIAL - Simple preparations like rat on a stick or mashed potatoes
TASK_EASY - Basic dishes like fried catfish or marinated steak
TASK_NORMAL - Complete meals like steak dinner
TASK_HARD - Complex dishes requiring greater skill

Some recipes may require special ingredients that can be obtained through 
hunting, foraging, or purchasing from shops. Thieves with the toxicity skill 
can also use cooking to prepare poisons from harvested reagents.

Failed cooking attempts may result in ruined ingredients or inedible food.
As your cooking skill improves, you'll gain access to more complex recipes
and have a higher success rate.

